   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the village of Freeport, county of Nassau,\nto alienate and discontinue the use of certain parklands",
    "basePrintNo": "S8541",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8541-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8541A\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the village of Freeport, county of\nNassau, to alienate and discontinue the use of certain parklands\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to remove a parkland easement on a\nproperty belonging to the Village of Freeport.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. provides for the removal of parkland easements on the proper-\nty known as Cleveland Avenue Field / Buffalo Avenue Field.\n\nSection 2. provides for a land swap in exchange of the removal of the\nparkland easement. Section 3. provides the coordinates of the property.\n\nSection 4. requires federal compliance.\n\nSection 5. is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Village of Freeport, accepted the conveyance by the County of Nassau\nof the park known as and by, \"Cow Meadow Field.\" A park of over 36\nacres, through Senate Bill 501372 and Assembly A7292 and signed by the\nGovernor on October 10, 2021 as Chap. 463. The Village has offered the\n\"Cow meadow Field,\" as a like kind exchange for the \"Cleveland\nAvenue/Buffalo Avenue Field.\" A parkland of 13 acres. Such consideration\nwould extend parkland within the Village of Freeport, provide for more\nrecreational and parkland benefits to the residents of the Village of\nFreeport, and would provide for the lifting of the Park and Recreational\nEasement on the \"Cleveland Avenue/Buffalo Avenue\" easement.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
